  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Ringfenced 1p Income Tax rise for NHS and social care; mental health parity with national waiting time standards; uprate working‑age benefits and scrap the two‑child limit/bedroom tax; build 300,000 homes/year with strong tenant protections; defence spend at 2% of GDP and maintain a minimum nuclear deterrent; enhance security cooperation (Europol/EAW); eliminate day‑to‑day deficit by 2020 and create an independent health/care budget watchdog; strong environmental/air quality and animal‑welfare measures. TEXT_G: Increase Scotland’s NHS budget and oppose privatisation; uprate benefits, scrap the two‑child cap and harsh sanctions, protect the pension triple lock; move toward a real Living Wage, ban exploitative zero‑hours, abolish tribunal fees; cancel nuclear weapons renewal and reinvest in conventional defence; prioritise renewables with moratoria on fracking; energy price cap for consumers; seek additional devolved powers and affirm the Scottish Parliament’s right to decide on a future independence referendum.",
